  "fairness": {
    "title": "How the dice work",
    "p1": "Every die has an equal 1 in 6 chance of landing on each face. Dice Den uses your phone's secure random number generator, the same kind used for encryption.",
    "p2": "The computer players roll the same dice, from the same generator. They never see future rolls, and the dice never change with the difficulty level.",
    "p3": "There are no lucky streaks, catch-up rolls or help: no player gets better dice when they are behind.",
    "p4": "Today's dice come from a fixed sequence for each date, so everyone who plays today gets exactly the same rolls in the same order.",
    "p5": "You can check all of this yourself: Stats shows every face you and the computer have rolled.",
